    "content": "I'll start by silently analyzing the codebase to understand its structure and identify vestigial web design business content.\n\n🔧 Tool: Task\nInput: {\n  \"description\": \"Explore codebase structure\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Explore this codebase thoroughly. I need to understand:\\n1. The overall project structure (all directories and key files)\\n2. What framework/tech stack is used\\n3. The purpose - it's supposed to be a starter template for small service business websites\\n\\nList ALL files, especially content files, config files, component files, and any data files. Use glob patterns like **/*.{astro,ts,tsx,js,jsx,json,md,mdx,css} to find everything. Also look at the root directory structure.\",\n  \"subagent_type\": \"Explore\",\n  \"run_in_background\": true\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Task\nInput: {\n  \"description\": \"Find web design content\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Search the entire codebase for any content related to a \\\"web design\\\" business. Look for:\\n1. Text mentioning \\\"web design\\\", \\\"web development\\\", \\\"website design\\\", \\\"websites that turn visitors into customers\\\"\\n2. References to building websites for clients\\n3. Service offerings related to web design/development\\n4. Any \\\"mini-website-mockup\\\" element or similar\\n5. Text like \\\"Fast-loading, search-friendly websites\\\"\\n6. Any portfolio or case study content about web design projects\\n7. Pricing for web design services\\n8. Testimonials about web design work\\n\\nUse grep to search for patterns like: \\\"web design\\\", \\\"website\\\", \\\"SEO\\\", \\\"search-friendly\\\", \\\"mockup\\\", \\\"portfolio\\\", \\\"visitors into customers\\\", \\\"fast-loading\\\", etc.\\n\\nReport ALL matches with file paths and line numbers, and the surrounding context.\",\n  \"subagent_type\": \"Explore\",\n  \"run_in_background\": true\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\C--Users-James-Repos-service-business\\\\tasks\\\\aca3bff.output\"\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: TaskOutput\nInput: {\n  \"task_id\": \"a2f54a0\",\n  \"block\": true,\n  \"timeout\": 30000\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\C--Users-James-Repos-service-business\\\\tasks\\\\a2f54a0.output\"\n}\nNow let me read the key files to understand the full scope of changes needed.\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\pages\\\\index.astro\"\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\HeroSection.astro\"\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\pages\\\\services.astro\"\n}\nNow let me read more of the affected files:\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\HeroSection.astro\",\n  \"limit\": 200\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\config\\\\blog.config.ts\"\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\types\\\\contact-form.ts\",\n  \"limit\": 200\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\types\\\\blog.ts\",\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\nLet me read a few more key files to complete my understanding:\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\HeroSection.astro\",\n  \"offset\": 200,\n  \"limit\": 200\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\config\\\\service-checklists.config.ts\",\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\config\\\\resources.config.ts\",\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\Breadcrumb.astro\",\n  \"limit\": 80\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\FeaturedProjectsPreview.astro\",\n  \"limit\": 80\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\BeforeAfterGallery.astro\",\n  \"limit\": 80\n}\nNow let me check a few more files to complete the picture:\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\types\\\\blog.ts\",\n  \"offset\": 200,\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\types\\\\service-checklist.ts\",\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\docs\\\\SEO_COMPONENT.md\",\n  \"limit\": 30\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\config\\\\seo.config.ts\",\n  \"limit\": 80\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\ContactForm.astro\",\n  \"offset\": 1230,\n  \"limit\": 30\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\config\\\\featured-projects.config.ts\",\n  \"limit\": 60\n}\nNow let me check the FAQ config to see if there's web-design content there too:\n\n🔧 Tool: Grep\nInput: {\n  \"pattern\": \"web.?design|website.?design|web development|websites that|Fast.?loading.*search|Houston Web|mini.?website|mockup|webDesign|web-design\",\n  \"output_mode\": \"files_with_matches\"\n}\nNow I have a comprehensive picture. Let me read the remaining key source files:\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\types\\\\blog.ts\",\n  \"offset\": 200,\n  \"limit\": 40\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\types\\\\service-checklist.ts\",\n  \"offset\": 180,\n  \"limit\": 70\n}\n\n🔧 Tool: Read\nInput: {\n  \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\James\\\\Repos\\\\service-business\\\\src\\\\components\\\\BlogFilter.astro\",\n  \"limit\": 30\n}\nI now have a thorough understanding of the codebase. Let me generate the specification.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Problem Statement\n\nThis repository was forked from a web design business site and is intended to serve as a generic starter template for small service businesses (e.g., plumbing, landscaping, restaurants). However, extensive vestigial content remains from the original web design business: service offerings for \"Website Design,\" \"Website Maintenance,\" \"Web Hosting,\" and \"Existing Website Support\"; a browser mockup element in the hero section showcasing a website; web-design-specific blog categories, tags, and default author references; and text like \"Fast-loading, search-friendly websites that turn visitors into customers.\"\n\n## 2. User Story\n\nAs a **developer using this starter template**, I want **all web-design-business-specific content removed or replaced with generic service business placeholders**, so that **I can quickly customize the template for any small service business without having to hunt down and clean up irrelevant web design references**.\n\n## 3. Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Happy Path**: GIVEN the template is freshly cloned, WHEN a developer reviews the content, THEN all text, service offerings, categories, and tags are generic/placeholder-based for a general service business with no web-design-specific references.\n- **Hero Mockup Removal**: GIVEN the HeroSection component, WHEN it renders, THEN there is no browser mockup element showing a mini-website preview (the entire mockup section is removed).\n- **Services Generalized**: GIVEN the services page, WHEN a user views it, THEN all five web-design-specific services (Website Design, Maintenance, Hosting, Existing Website Support, Business Process Automation) are replaced with three generic placeholder services.\n- **Tags & Categories**: GIVEN the blog, resource, and checklist configs, WHEN referenced, THEN web-design-specific tags/categories are replaced with generic service-business tags/categories.\n- **Contact Form**: GIVEN the contact form, WHEN a user views project types, THEN options are generic service inquiry types, not web-design project types.\n- **Edge Case - Houston Specific**: GIVEN location references like \"Serving the Greater Houston Area,\" WHEN rendered, THEN these are replaced with generic placeholders like \"Serving Your Local Area.\"\n- **Error Handling**: GIVEN that some files are documentation (`.md`), WHEN these reference web design examples, THEN examples are updated to generic service business context.\n\n## 4. Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Affected Files | `src/components/HeroSection.astro`, `src/pages/services.astro`, `src/pages/index.astro`, `src/types/contact-form.ts`, `src/types/blog.ts`, `src/types/service-checklist.ts`, `src/config/blog.config.ts`, `src/config/resources.config.ts`, `src/config/service-checklists.config.ts`, `src/components/FeaturedProjectsPreview.astro`, `src/components/BeforeAfterGallery.astro`, `src/components/Breadcrumb.astro`, `src/components/ContactForm.astro`, `src/config/seo.config.ts`, `src/docs/SEO_COMPONENT.md` |\n| Dependencies | None (all changes are content/text) |\n| Constraints | Must preserve existing component architecture, props interfaces, and CSS; only content/text changes |\n| Patterns to Follow | Existing TODO/placeholder patterns already used in `index.astro` (e.g., \"Service One\", \"Your Business Name\") |\n\n## 5. Non-Goals\n\n- **Not** changing any visual design, CSS styling, or component architecture\n- **Not** removing the overall site structure (services page, blog, portfolio, contact form still exist)\n- **Not** changing configuration fields that are already blank/placeholder (e.g., empty `seoConfig` fields)\n- **Not** modifying `.automaker/` directory or test files\n- **Not** changing actual functional code logic, only content strings\n\n## 6. Implementation Tasks\n\n```tasks\n## Phase 1: Hero Section & Homepage Cleanup\n- [ ] T001: Remove the entire browser mockup element (hero__mockup div and all children, lines ~133-333) from HeroSection.astro, plus all associated CSS styles for mockup classes | File: src/components/HeroSection.astro\n- [ ] T002: Replace web-design-specific default trust badges (\"Fast & Search-Friendly Sites\") and default example text in HeroSection.astro comment/docblock | File: src/components/HeroSection.astro\n- [ ] T003: Replace \"Serving the Greater Houston Area\" location cue with generic placeholder text | File: src/components/HeroSection.astro\n- [ ] T004: Update homepage index.astro icon variable names from webDesign/existingWebsite to generic names, and fix icon key references | File: src/pages/index.astro\n\n## Phase 2: Services Page Overhaul\n- [ ] T005: Replace all 5 web-design-specific services on services.astro with 3 generic placeholder services (Service One, Service Two, Service Three) with placeholder descriptions, benefits, and pricing | File: src/pages/services.astro\n- [ ] T006: Update services page hero visual preview cards to match the new 3 generic services instead of showing Website Design/Maintenance/Automation/Site Support cards | File: src/pages/services.astro\n- [ ] T007: Remove extra service detail sections (keeping only 3) and update section HTML to reference the 3 generic services | File: src/pages/services.astro\n\n## Phase 3: Contact Form & Type Definitions\n- [ ] T008: Replace web-design-specific ProjectType values and labels with generic service business inquiry types (e.g., 'service-inquiry', 'estimate-request', 'maintenance-request', 'consultation', 'other') | File: src/types/contact-form.ts\n- [ ] T009: Update ContactForm.astro formatProjectType labels to match new generic types | File: src/components/ContactForm.astro\n\n## Phase 4: Blog, Resources & Checklist Configs\n- [ ] T010: Replace web-design-specific blog categories with generic service business categories; update BlogCategory type and BLOG_CATEGORIES array | File: src/types/blog.ts\n- [ ] T011: Update DEFAULT_AUTHOR in blog.ts from \"Houston Web Services\" to generic placeholder | File: src/types/blog.ts\n- [ ] T012: Rename web-design tags to generic service tags in blog.config.ts COMMON_TAGS | File: src/config/blog.config.ts\n- [ ] T013: Rename web-design tags to generic service tags in resources.config.ts COMMON_RESOURCE_TAGS | File: src/config/resources.config.ts\n- [ ] T014: Rename web-design tags and ServiceType values in service-checklists.config.ts and service-checklist.ts | File: src/config/service-checklists.config.ts\n- [ ] T015: Update ServiceType type and SERVICE_TYPES/SERVICE_TYPE_LABELS in service-checklist.ts to use generic service types | File: src/types/service-checklist.ts\n\n## Phase 5: Component Default Text & Breadcrumbs\n- [ ] T016: Update FeaturedProjectsPreview.astro default subheading from \"web design and development\" to generic text | File: src/components/FeaturedProjectsPreview.astro\n- [ ] T017: Update BeforeAfterGallery.astro default subheading from \"web design and development services\" to generic text | File: src/components/BeforeAfterGallery.astro\n- [ ] T018: Update Breadcrumb.astro pathNameMap to remove 'website-design' and add generic service paths | File: src/components/Breadcrumb.astro\n\n## Phase 6: SEO Config & Documentation\n- [ ] T019: Update seo.config.ts makesOffer/knowsAbout example comments to use generic service business examples instead of web design examples | File: src/config/seo.config.ts\n- [ ] T020: Update SEO_COMPONENT.md documentation examples from \"Houston Web Services\" and web design references to generic service business examples | File: src/docs/SEO_COMPONENT.md\n```\n\n## 7. Success Metrics\n\n- Zero occurrences of \"web design,\" \"website design,\" \"web development,\" \"Houston Web Services,\" or \"Fast-loading, search-friendly\" in any source file under `src/`\n- The hero mockup browser element is completely removed from the DOM\n- All service offerings use generic placeholder names (Service One, Two, Three)\n- Contact form project types are generic service inquiry types\n- Blog categories and tags are generic (no web-design-specific categories)\n- Template builds successfully with `npm run build`\n\n## 8. Risks & Mitigations\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|------------|\n| Breaking TypeScript type unions when changing ProjectType/BlogCategory values | Update all locations referencing the old string literal values simultaneously |\n| CSS orphan rules after mockup removal | Remove all associated CSS selectors for mockup classes |\n| Missed references in deeply nested files | Use grep search to verify zero remaining web-design references after all changes |\n| Build breakage from type mismatches | Run build verification after all changes |",
    "generatedAt": "2026-01-31T20:39:33.330Z",
